    "title": "It Is Drug Users Who Are Killing Themselves - Whatfinger News Quick Hits",
    "text": "Fentanyl is a synthetic opioid pain reliever approved by the Food and Drug (FDA) for treating severe pain. It is a Schedule II narcotic under the Controlled Substances Act (CSA) that is said to be 50 times more potent than heroin and 100 times more potent than morphine. (It is interesting that until recently, marijuana was classified as a Schedule I drug.)\nThe U.S. Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) is being criticized for intentionally allowing hundreds of thousands fentanyl pills to cross the New Mexico border from 2023-2025.\nRead Full Article: https://www.lewrockwell.com/2026/07/laurence-m-vance/it-is-drug-users-who-are-killing-themselves/",
    "summary": "Fentanyl is a synthetic opioid pain reliever approved by the Food and Drug (FDA) for treating severe pain. It is a Schedule II narcotic under the Controlled Substances Act (CSA) that is said to be 50 times more potent than heroin and 100 times more potent than morphine. (It is interesting that until recently, marijuana was classified as a Schedule I drug.) The U.S. Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) is being criticized for intentionally allowing hundreds of thousands fentanyl pills to cross the New Mexico border from 2023-2025.",
